Subject: [PATCH] wifi: learn country from scan results when cellular is unavailable

On a Wi-Fi-only device with no telephony country, ServiceWifiResources left
config_wifiUpdateCountryCodeFromScanResultGeneric false, so the 5 GHz upper
channels (149-165) were filtered and some APs (e.g. one on channel 153) never
appeared in scans. Enable Android's existing scan-based country fallback.
Telephony country is still preferred and weak/contradictory beacons are still
rejected; no fixed country is forced.

A device-tree static overlay cannot change this value because ServiceWifiResources
ships inside the com.android.wifi mainline APEX, which does not consume
DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS. The module is built from source in this tree, so set the
compiled default directly. The resource is overlayable under policy
odm|product|system|vendor, so a product/system RRO is the alternative.
---
 service/ServiceWifiResources/res/values/config.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/service/ServiceWifiResources/res/values/config.xml b/service/ServiceWifiResources/res/values/config.xml
index 200320a..0ac004c 100644
--- a/service/ServiceWifiResources/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/service/ServiceWifiResources/res/values/config.xml
@@ -1279,7 +1279,7 @@
          no telephony country code. This is applied to all generic cases and might require the
          regulatory approval (for example, FCC pre-approval is required according to "594280 D01
          Software Configuration Control v02r01").-->
-    <bool translatable="false" name ="config_wifiUpdateCountryCodeFromScanResultGeneric">false</bool>
+    <bool translatable="false" name ="config_wifiUpdateCountryCodeFromScanResultGeneric">true</bool>
     <!-- Boolean indication whether enable VDBG for more detailed log when Wi-Fi aware verbose
     logging is enabled -->
     <bool translatable="false" name ="config_aware_vdbg_enable_on_verbose_logging">false</bool>
